From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: cdns-dphy: stop the TX state machine in power_off

cdns_dphy_power_on() starts the startup state machine by setting
DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN, and cdns_dphy_power_off() never cleared it, so a
power_off did not actually stop the PHY. Measured on Astrial H15:
DPHY_CMN_SSM (0x7c01a020) reads 0x00000201 both before and after a
power_off.

Mainline clears the bit in power_off, after gating the clocks. Do the
same, in the same order.

Clearing the bit by hand with devmem on a board without this patch did
not bring a dead panel back, but that experiment read the lane ready
flags without clearing them first (see 0015), so it is not evidence
either way. This is alignment with mainline, not a claimed fix.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
@@ -339,11 +339,16 @@
 static int cdns_dphy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
 {
 	struct cdns_dphy *dphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	u32 reg;
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->pll_ref_clk);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->psm_clk);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(dphy->esc_clk);
 
+	/* Stop TX state machine. */
+	reg = readl(dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
+	writel(reg & ~DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN, dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
+
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(&phy->dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&phy->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&phy->dev);
